  <h1>32:18 Research</h1>
</BarcelonaReveal>

<Layout
	title="About"
	description=""
	pubDate={new Date('September 13, 2026')}
>
	<p>
		My primary concern is a growing wealth and class 
		divide in America, one that may be driving a 
		wedge deep into our society. Despite being the 
		wealthiest nation on earth, I suspect that wealth 
		increasingly benefits only a select few. Housing sits 
		at the center of this: for many Americans, it has 
		stopped functioning primarily as shelter and started 
		functioning as an investment vehicle.
	</p>

	<p>
		Housing, like food and water, is a basic human need, 
		and I think a society's treatment of that need is 
		worth measuring carefully.
	</p>

	<p>
		32:18 exists to test this concern with data rather 
		than argument. My approach is simple: form a thesis, 
		pull public data, clean it, and lay out the results, 
		graphs, numbers, whatever the data shows. I draw 
		conclusions from what I find, and publish the source 
		data alongside every piece so anyone can reproduce the 
		analysis or look at it from another angle.
	</p>

</Layout>
